"""Approximate a negative comma-boundary signal using readable text features.
For lone ASCII commas, longer comma-free spans strengthen the negative signal;
nearby commas, short introductions, and open brackets weaken it. Previous
spacing and capitalization add small corrections. A document-leading comma
is a special positive case. Other comma forms use punctuation-shape estimates,
semicolons are mildly negative, and all other tokens are predicted as zero.
Word-specific variations in the real component are intentionally omitted.
