The component is strongly negative on commas (ASCII ',' and fullwidth '，') and near zero
everywhere else. Its size on a comma depends on two things a reader can see in the text:

* How far back the previous comma is. A comma that comes right after another comma (a
  list such as "a, b, c") is weak; one that comes after a long stretch with no comma is
  strong.
* How far into the sentence the comma falls. A comma right after a one- or two-word opener
  ("So,", "But,", "Wait,") is weak; one that closes a longer introductory phrase ("After
  his condition remained unchanged,") is strong.

Commas glued to a closing bracket or quote ("),", '",') are moderately negative.

The program predicts the component's activation: negative on commas, scaled down by the
two gap rules, and 0 elsewhere.
