Its largest negative outputs mark 'tune' and its inflections. It also
responds to musical harmony, symmetry, trimming and adjustment vocabulary.
Some response is spelling-based: the endings 'une', 'unes', etc. fire even
inside unrelated words, and French 'une' fires as a whole word. Split
spellings of fine-tuning get a stronger response. Everything else is near
zero. This is a lexical approximation, not a musical-topic classifier.
"""
