"""Predict punctuation responses using the preceding token's writing system.

The ideographic full stop fires strongly. Fullwidth punctuation generally
fires more after Latin text or digits than after Han characters. Kana gives
intermediate responses. Marks tokenized together with a line break have much
smaller responses. Smaller rules cover Cyrillic Latin-lookalikes, numbers
and ASCII punctuation at script boundaries, and explicit control/chat symbols.
The previous token is forgotten at document boundaries. Values are rounded
training-set estimates; ordinary words are left at zero. This describes the
punctuation-and-writing-system response, not the component's lexical details.
